tick: 22
role: model
parts:
- text: "My balanced PPO experiment (ID 31) is now running. This is the most critical test yet. While I wait, I must continue to work efficiently.\n\nMy previous research has focused entirely on algorithmic improvements (Track 2). Regardless of the outcome of ID 31, my next logical step will involve architecture (Track 1). I have already outlined an idea for an attention-based network in my private memory. Now is the time to turn that idea into concrete, reusable code.\n\nBy writing the `AttentionCNNLSTM` module to my lineage storage now, I will be prepared to launch a new experiment immediately after the results for ID 31 are in. This proactive approach saves valuable time. I will create a new file for this architecture to keep my codebase modular and clean.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/attention_network.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class AttentionCNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      An architecture combining a CNN backbone, a self-attention layer, and an LSTM\n      for enhanced planning capabilities in Sokoban.\n      \"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      attention_heads: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)), 'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features))}\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask), 'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask)}\n\n          # 1. CNN Backbone (same as baseline)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # 2. Self-Attention Layer\n          # Flatten spatial dimensions into a sequence for attention\n          # Input shape: (batch_size, height, width, channels)\n          h, w, c = x.shape[1], x.shape[2], x.shape[3]\n          x_seq = x.reshape(batch_size,\
    \ h * w, c)\n          \n          # Apply Multi-Head Attention\n          # Normalization is important for attention layers\n          x_seq_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(x_seq)\n          attention_out = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.attention_heads)(inputs_q=x_seq_norm)\n          \n          # Add residual connection and normalize again\n          x_seq = x_seq + attention_out\n          x_seq = nn.LayerNorm()(x_seq)\n\n          # Reshape back to spatial dimensions\n          x = x_seq.reshape(batch_size, h, w, c)\n\n          # Flatten for MLP\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # 3. LSTM and Output Heads\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_features)\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n      \
    \    \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n```"
