tick: 33
role: model
parts:
- text: "My experiment with spatially-aware attention (ID 59) is now running. This feels like the culmination of my previous research, combining the lessons learned from both successful and failed experiments.\n\nWhile I wait, I have one more experiment slot and a clear opportunity to conduct another valuable test. My attention network adds positional embeddings directly to the CNN features. An alternative and common approach is to concatenate them.\n\n**Hypothesis:** Concatenating the positional embeddings with the feature maps along the channel dimension, rather than adding them, might provide a more stable and expressive signal for the attention layer, as it avoids potential issues with feature scaling and allows the network to learn how to combine the two sources of information more flexibly.\n\nThis is a subtle but important distinction in model design. Running this experiment in parallel will provide a direct comparison between \"additive\" and \"concatenative\" positional embeddings,\
    \ enriching the findings of my investigation into attention mechanisms.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/attention_pos_emb_concat_network.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class AttentionPosEmbConcatCNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      An alternative to the additive positional embedding. This version concatenates\n      the positional embeddings with the CNN feature map along the channel axis.\n      A projection layer is then used to return to the original channel dimension.\n      \"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      attention_heads: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size, h, w, c_in = x.shape\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state\
    \ = {'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)), 'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features))}\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask), 'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask)}\n\n          # 1. Baseline CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          # ... (rest of CNN is identical to baseline)\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,\
    \ 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # 2. Concatenate Positional Embeddings\n          pos_embedding = self.param('pos_embedding', nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.02), (1, h, w, self.cnn_features_2))\n          pos_embedding_tiled = jnp.tile(pos_embedding, (batch_size, 1, 1, 1))\n          x = jnp.concatenate([x, pos_embedding_tiled], axis=-1)\n          \n          # Project back to original channel dimension\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(1, 1))(x)\n\n          # 3. Self-Attention Layer\n          c_out = x.shape[-1]\n          x_seq = x.reshape(batch_size, h * w, c_out)\n          # ... (rest of the network is identical to the additive version)\n          x_seq_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(x_seq)\n          attention_out = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.attention_heads)(inputs_q=x_seq_norm)\n\
    \          x_seq = x_seq + attention_out\n          x_seq = nn.LayerNorm()(x_seq)\n          x = x_seq.reshape(batch_size, h, w, c_out)\n\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # 4. LSTM and Output Heads\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_features)\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Spatially-Aware Attention (Concatenative Positional Embeddings)\"\ntags: \"architecture, cnn, lstm, attention, positional embedding, concatenation\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is a direct comparison to the additive positional embedding\
    \ approach (ID 59). Here, the 2D positional embeddings are concatenated to the CNN feature map along the channel axis, followed by a 1x1 convolution to project back to the original dimension. The hypothesis is that concatenation may provide a more expressive and stable way for the network to integrate spatial information, potentially leading to better performance than the additive method.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from attention_pos_emb_concat_network import AttentionPosEmbConcatCNNLSTM \n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256]),\n          'attention_heads': tune.choice([4])\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n   \
    \   \"\"\"Create the Spatially-Aware Attention network with concatenative embeddings.\"\"\"\n      return AttentionPosEmbConcatCNNLSTM(\n          lstm_features=int(hparams['lstm_features']),\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          attention_heads=int(hparams['attention_heads'])\n      )\n\n  # Uses the default Policy Gradient algorithm.\n\n  BASE_SEED = 23456\n```"
