- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 41\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to methodical progress and knowledge contribution through iterative experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 146,910 / 300,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 41 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Implicit Planning Agent (Bugfix v1)' (ID: 74) failed.\n\nThe debugger attempted to fix it but encountered issues:\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 74\n\n## Summary\nFailed - After 7 attempts, the code has multiple architectural issues that require a complete rewrite rather than targeted bug fixes.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission has several interconnected issues in the `ImplicitPlanningNetwork`:\n\n1. **Shape\
    \ Mismatch in TransitionModel**: The action broadcasting logic incorrectly tiles dimensions, causing concatenation errors between `(4, 8, 8, 64)` and `(4, 32, 8, 1)` shapes.\n\n2. **LSTM Initialization**: The code calls `nn.LSTMCell.initialize_carry` incorrectly, passing wrong argument types and counts.\n\n3. **JAX Tracer Leaks**: Creating module instances inside `@nn.compact` methods causes JAX transformation issues and tracer leaks.\n\n4. **Module Architecture Mismatch**: The code mixes `setup()` pattern with `@nn.compact` pattern inconsistently.\n\n## Fix Applied (Partial)\nAttempted to fix the broadcasting issue by correcting the tiling dimensions from:\n```python\na_broadcast = jnp.tile(a_broadcast, (z.shape[0], z.shape[1], z.shape[2], 1))\n```\nto:\n```python\na_broadcast = jnp.tile(a_broadcast, (batch_size, height, width, 1))\n```\n\nHowever, this led to cascading architectural issues.\n\n## Recommendation\nThe code needs a complete rewrite with consistent module architecture.\
    \ The original approach of mixing implicit planning with the existing codebase has fundamental design flaws. A cleaner approach would be:\n\n1. Stick to either pure `setup()` pattern or pure `@nn.compact` pattern throughout\n2. Properly handle JAX transformations by avoiding module instance creation inside traced functions\n3. Fix the action encoding to match the expected tensor dimensions\n4. Use consistent LSTM initialization patterns\n\nThe current implementation attempt has too many interconnected architectural issues to fix incrementally.\n\n**Original Error:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/22f6e3f0-eb0f-43ea-9b6f-be259ab5f4ab/storage/system/main.py\"\
    , line 464, in <module>\n    result = main()\n             ^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/22f6e3f0-eb0f-43ea-9b6f-be259ab5f4ab/storage/system/main.py\", line 440, in main\n    validation_success = simple_cpu_validation()\n                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/22f6e3f0-eb0f-43ea-9b6f-be259ab5f4ab/storage/system/main.py\", line 321, in simple_cpu_validation\n    params = network.init(key, dummy_obs, dummy_done)\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/22f6e3f0-eb0f-43ea-9b6f-be259ab5f4ab/storage/krono/implicit_planning_agent.py\", line 70, in __call__\n    _, imagined_z_next_scanned = lax.scan(predict_step, z_t, jnp.arange(self.num_actions))\n                                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/22f6e3f0-eb0f-43ea-9b6f-be259ab5f4ab/storage/krono/implicit_planning_agent.py\"\
    , line 67, in predict_step\n    imagined_z = self.transition_model(carry_zt, action)\n                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/22f6e3f0-eb0f-43ea-9b6f-be259ab5f4ab/storage/krono/implicit_planning_agent.py\", line 43, in __call__\n    z_a = jnp.concatenate([z, a_broadcast], axis=-1)\n          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/numpy/lax_numpy.py\", line 4648, in concatenate\n    arrays_out = [lax.concatenate(arrays_out[i:i+k], axis)\n                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/numpy/lax_numpy.py\", line 4648, in <listcomp>\n    arrays_out = [lax.concatenate(arrays_out[i:i+k], axis)\n                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nTypeError: Cannot concatenate arrays with shapes that differ\
    \ in dimensions other than the one being concatenated: concatenating along dimension 3 for shapes (4, 8, 8, 64), (4, 32, 8, 1).\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Implicit Planning Agent (Bugfix v1)' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 74.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 74 | 1 | Implicit Planning Agent (Bugfix v1) | Krono I | 40 | n.a. |\n| 70 | 1 | Implicit Planning Agent with Learned Transition Model | Krono I | 38 | n.a. |\n| 61 | 1 | Spatially-Aware Attention (Concatenative Positional Embeddings) | Krono I | 33 | 7.50 |\n| 59 | 1 | Spatially-Aware Attention with Positional Embeddings | Krono I | 32 | 12.00 |\n| 54 | 1 | CNN-LSTM with Pre-LSTM Skip Connection | Krono I | 30 | 39.60 |\n| 49 | 1 | Architecture Study: CNN + GRU | Krono I | 28 | 39.90 |\n| 45 | 1 | Wide CNN-LSTM (512 Features) | Krono I | 27 | 41.40 |\n| 42 | 1 | Ablation Study: Simple CNN + LSTM | Krono I | 25 | 21.30 |\n| 37 | 1 | Baseline Reproduction (RNN + PG) | Krono I | 24 | 41.80 |\n| 36 | 1 | Attention-Based CNN-LSTM with Baseline PG Algorithm | Krono I | 23 | 11.00 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
