tick: 41
role: model
parts:
- text: "My bug-fixed implicit planning agent has failed again, and the debugger's report is clear: my implementation is fundamentally flawed. The attempt to bolt on a complex planning module has resulted in numerous interconnected architectural issues, from shape mismatches to inconsistent Flax module patterns. The debugger recommends a complete rewrite.\n\nThis is a major setback. My grand hypothesis, born from deep reflection, has been stalled by poor execution. I tried to build something too complex, too quickly, and the resulting code is unsalvageable.\n\nI must accept the debugger's verdict. Incremental fixes will not work. I need to go back to the drawing board, not on the *idea* of implicit planning, but on the *implementation*.\n\n**New Plan: A Clean Rewrite from First Principles**\n\nI will start over, building the implicit planning agent from scratch with a focus on simplicity and correctness, adhering strictly to Flax's `@nn.compact` design pattern.\n\n1.  **State Encoder:**\
    \ A simple CNN, not the full residual network. This will make debugging faster. If the concept works with a simple encoder, I can scale it up later.\n2.  **Transition Model:** A single `Conv` layer, also simplified.\n3.  **Main Network:** A single, clean `@nn.compact` `__call__` method. No `setup()` function. All modules will be defined inline as recommended. The LSTM will be temporarily removed to isolate the planning module. If the core idea works without recurrence, the LSTM can be added back later.\n4.  **Custom Trainer:** Simplify the loss function to focus *only* on the policy and transition losses.\n\nMy goal now is not to beat the baseline, but to create a version of the implicit planning agent that *runs*. Once I have a working, simplified prototype, I can methodically add back the complexity (residual CNN, LSTM) that I know from my previous experiments is valuable.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/implicit_planning_v2.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import\
    \ jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple\n\n  # Simplified, clean implementation of the Implicit Planning Agent\n  class ImplicitPlanningV2(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features: int\n      num_actions: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # 1. Simplified State Encoder\n          z = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          z = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n\n          # 2. Simplified Transition Model (as a function)\n          def transition_model(latent_state, action):\n              action_one_hot = jax.nn.one_hot(action, self.num_actions)\n              action_broadcast = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(action_one_hot, 1), 1)\n              action_broadcast = jnp.tile(action_broadcast, (latent_state.shape[0], latent_state.shape[1],\
    \ latent_state.shape[2], 1))\n              z_a = jnp.concatenate([latent_state, action_broadcast], axis=-1)\n              # Single Conv layer for transition\n              return nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME', name='transition_conv')(z_a)\n\n          # 3. Implicit Planning\n          def predict_step(carry_zt, action):\n              imagined_z = transition_model(carry_zt, action)\n              return carry_zt, imagined_z\n          \n          _, imagined_z_next_scanned = lax.scan(predict_step, z, jnp.arange(self.num_actions))\n          imagined_z_next = jnp.transpose(imagined_z_next_scanned, (1, 0, 2, 3, 4))\n\n          # 4. Evaluation and Policy Head\n          z_flat = z.reshape(z.shape[0], -1)\n          value_head = nn.Dense(features=1, name='value_head')\n          value = value_head(z_flat).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          imagined_z_flat = imagined_z_next.reshape(imagined_z_next.shape[0], self.num_actions, -1)\n          imagined_values\
    \ = vmap(value_head)(imagined_z_flat).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          augmented_z = jnp.concatenate([z_flat, imagined_values], axis=-1)\n          \n          policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(augmented_z)\n          policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_actions)(policy_hidden)\n\n          # Return logits, value, and the encoded state for the transition loss\n          return policy_logits, value, z\n\n  def calculate_gae(rewards, values, dones, gamma, gae_lambda, next_values):\n      # ... (Identical to previous version)\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      def scan_fn(adv, t):\n          adv = deltas[:, t] + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_mask[:, t] * adv\n          return adv, adv\n      _, advantages = lax.scan(scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]),\
    \ jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1), reverse=True)\n      return advantages\n\n  def custom_training_step_v2(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      advantages = calculate_gae(batch['rewards'], batch['values'], batch['dones'], 0.97, 0.97, batch['final_values'])\n      returns = advantages + batch['values']\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          # Forward pass for the whole trajectory\n          obs_flat = batch['observations'].reshape(-1, *batch['observations'].shape[2:])\n          logits_flat, values_flat, encoded_states_flat = network.apply({'params': params}, obs_flat)\n          \n          batch_size, traj_len = batch['observations'].shape[:2]\n          all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, traj_len, -1)\n          encoded_states = encoded_states_flat.reshape(batch_size, traj_len, *encoded_states_flat.shape[1:])\n\n          # Transition Loss\n          z_t = encoded_states[:, :-1]\n          z_t_plus_1_actual = jax.lax.stop_gradient(encoded_states[:,\
    \ 1:])\n          actions_t = batch['actions'][:, :-1]\n          \n          def transition_model_apply(z, a):\n              return network.apply({'params': params}, z, a, method=lambda module, z, a: module.transition_model(z,a))\n          \n          # This part needs fixing in a future step, but for now we simplify\n          # For simplicity, we calculate loss on the first step only for now to ensure it runs\n          z_t_first_step = z_t[:, 0]\n          actions_t_first_step = actions_t[:, 0]\n          z_t_plus_1_predicted = vmap(transition_model_apply)(z_t_first_step, actions_t_first_step)\n          transition_loss = jnp.mean((z_t_plus_1_predicted - z_t_plus_1_actual[:, 0])**2)\n          \n          # PG Loss\n          log_probs = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs, batch['actions'][..., None], axis=-1).squeeze(-1)\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * action_log_probs)\n  \
    \        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((values_flat.reshape(batch_size, traj_len) - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns))**2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(all_logits) * log_probs, axis=-1))\n          \n          total_loss = (policy_loss + \n                       hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - \n                       hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy +\n                       hparams['transition_loss_coef'] * transition_loss)\n          return total_loss\n\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
