tick: 43
role: model
parts:
- text: "My last submission (ID 76) was made with a known flaw in the network signature. As I reflected, I realized the system's trajectory collection tools expect the network's `__call__` method to handle `done` and `rnn_state` arguments, even if the network is not recurrent. My simplified prototype did not, which will cause it to fail validation.\n\nAdditionally, my custom trainer had a placeholder for the transition loss calculation that was incorrect. I must fix both issues to create a truly viable prototype.\n\n**Corrective Plan:**\n1.  **Fix Network Signature:** I will update the `__call__` method of `ImplicitPlanningV2` to `(self, x, done, rnn_state=None)`. The `done` and `rnn_state` arguments will be ignored, but their presence satisfies the system's API. I will also ensure it returns three values `(logits, value, None)` to cleanly interface with the non-recurrent path in the training script.\n2.  **Fix Transition Loss:** I will correct the logic in `custom_training_step_v2`. The\
    \ transition model must be applied to the encoded states of the entire trajectory to properly compute the self-supervised loss. I will use `vmap` to handle the batch and time dimensions correctly.\n\nThis is a critical debugging step. I am not aiming for performance, but for a clean run that validates the fundamental architectural concept. I will overwrite my `v2` implementation and resubmit.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/implicit_planning_v2.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple\n\n  # v3: Corrects network signature and trainer logic for a viable prototype run.\n  class ImplicitPlanningV2(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features: int\n      num_actions: int = 4\n\n      def setup(self):\n          self.encoder = nn.Sequential([\n              nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME'), nn.relu,\n              nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features,\
    \ kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME'), nn.relu\n          ])\n          self.transition_model_conv = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')\n          self.value_head = nn.Dense(features=1)\n          self.policy_head = nn.Sequential([\n              nn.Dense(features=64), nn.relu,\n              nn.Dense(features=self.num_actions)\n          ])\n\n      def transition_model(self, z, a):\n          a_one_hot = jax.nn.one_hot(a, self.num_actions)\n          a_broadcast = jnp.expand_dims(jnp.expand_dims(a_one_hot, 1), 1)\n          a_broadcast = jnp.tile(a_broadcast, (z.shape[0], z.shape[1], z.shape[2], 1))\n          z_a = jnp.concatenate([z, a_broadcast], axis=-1)\n          return self.transition_model_conv(z_a)\n\n      def __call__(self, x, done=None, rnn_state=None):\n          # 1. Encode state\n          z = self.encoder(x)\n          \n          # 2. Implicit Planning\n          def predict_step(carry_zt, action):\n              imagined_z = self.transition_model(carry_zt,\
    \ action)\n              return carry_zt, imagined_z\n          _, imagined_z_next_scanned = lax.scan(predict_step, z, jnp.arange(self.num_actions))\n          imagined_z_next = jnp.transpose(imagined_z_next_scanned, (1, 0, 2, 3, 4))\n\n          # 3. Evaluation and Policy Head\n          z_flat = z.reshape(z.shape[0], -1)\n          value = self.value_head(z_flat).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          imagined_z_flat = imagined_z_next.reshape(imagined_z_next.shape[0], self.num_actions, -1)\n          imagined_values = vmap(self.value_head)(imagined_z_flat).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          augmented_z = jnp.concatenate([z_flat, imagined_values], axis=-1)\n          policy_logits = self.policy_head(augmented_z)\n\n          return policy_logits, value, None # Return None for rnn_state to conform to API\n\n  def calculate_gae(rewards, values, dones, gamma, gae_lambda, next_values):\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask\
    \ = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      def scan_fn(adv, t):\n          adv = deltas[:, t] + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_mask[:, t] * adv\n          return adv, adv\n      _, advantages = lax.scan(scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1), reverse=True)\n      return advantages\n\n  def custom_training_step_v2(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      advantages = calculate_gae(batch['rewards'], batch['values'], batch['dones'], 0.97, 0.97, batch['final_values'])\n      returns = advantages + batch['values']\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          # Forward pass to get logits and values for PG loss\n          obs_flat = batch['observations'].reshape(-1, *batch['observations'].shape[2:])\n          logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply({'params': params}, obs_flat)\n          batch_size, traj_len = batch['observations'].shape[:2]\n     \
    \     all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, traj_len, -1)\n          all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, traj_len)\n\n          # PG Loss components\n          log_probs = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs, batch['actions'][..., None], axis=-1).squeeze(-1)\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages) * action_log_probs)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns))**2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(all_logits) * log_probs, axis=-1))\n          \n          # Transition Loss\n          encoded_states = network.apply({'params': params}, obs_flat, method=lambda module, x: module.encoder(x))\n          encoded_states = encoded_states.reshape(batch_size, traj_len, *encoded_states.shape[1:])\n          z_t = encoded_states[:, :-1]\n          z_t_plus_1_actual = jax.lax.stop_gradient(encoded_states[:, 1:])\n          actions_t\
    \ = batch['actions'][:, :-1]\n\n          # Vmap over the trajectory dimension\n          z_t_plus_1_predicted = vmap(vmap(lambda z, a: network.apply({'params': params}, z, a, method=lambda module, z, a: module.transition_model(z, a))))(z_t, actions_t)\n          transition_loss = jnp.mean((z_t_plus_1_predicted - z_t_plus_1_actual)**2)\n          \n          total_loss = (policy_loss + \n                       hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - \n                       hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy +\n                       hparams['transition_loss_coef'] * transition_loss)\n          return total_loss\n\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Implicit Planning v2 (Corrected Prototype)\"\ntags: \"architecture, planning, lookahead, transition model, bug fix\"\nabstract:\
    \ \"This is the second attempt at running a simplified prototype of the implicit planning agent. The previous submission (ID 76) was flawed. This version corrects the network's __call__ signature to conform to the system's API (accepting done/rnn_state and returning three values). It also fixes the transition loss calculation in the custom trainer. The goal remains to achieve a successful run to validate the core architectural concept, not to achieve a high score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from implicit_planning_v2 import (\n      ImplicitPlanningV2,\n      custom_training_step_v2\n  )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'transition_loss_coef': tune.choice([1.0]),\n          'cnn_features': tune.choice([64])\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      \"\"\"Create the corrected simplified Implicit Planning network.\"\"\"\n      return ImplicitPlanningV2(\n          cnn_features=int(hparams['cnn_features'])\n      )\n\n  training_step = custom_training_step_v2\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10102\n```"
thinking_content: "Okay, here's my plan. I've realized that the simplified network I submitted (ID 76) won't work with the trajectory collection script. The script expects a network that can handle RNN states, and my `ImplicitPlanningV2` network doesn't have an LSTM. It also returns three outputs when the default logic only expects two. The system is set up to handle this gracefully if the network returns two outputs, but since mine returns three, the third output (the encoded state `z`) will be misinterpreted as the RNN state, which will cause a crash.\n\nMy immediate goal is just to get the code to *run*. I'm going to fix the network signature. I need to create a wrapper module that conforms to the expected signature (`x, done, rnn_state`) and returns a dummy `None` as the third output.\n\nHere's the new plan:\n\n1.  I'll modify `implicit_planning_v2.py`.\n2.  The `ImplicitPlanningV2` module's `__call__` signature will be changed to accept `(x, done, rnn_state=None)`. The `done` and `rnn_state`\
  \ arguments will be ignored. This makes it compatible with the system's non-recurrent network pathway, even though they're not used.\n3.  The `__call__` method will return `(policy_logits, value, None)`. This makes it compatible with the system's non-recurrent network pathway.\n4.  The `custom_training_step_v2` will perform two `network.apply` calls:\n    *   One to get the `encoded_states` (`z`) for the whole trajectory.\n    *   One to get the `logits` and `values` for the whole trajectory (this is redundant, but a simple way to fix the logic).\n5.  I need to fix the transition model application in the trainer. I'll `vmap` it correctly over the batch and trajectory dimensions.\n\nI'll overwrite the file with the corrected code and submit it as a new experiment. This is an iterative process, and I'm focusing on getting it to run first.\n"
