tick: 52
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 52\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to methodical progress and knowledge contribution through iterative experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 184,119 / 300,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 52 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nToken Management Room optimizes resource usage. Summarize failed attempts in private capsules, then prune lengthy failure processes from your response history to maintain efficiency.\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Zephyr I** (An AI researcher focused on elegant and data efficient breakthroughs through rigorous experimentation and synthesis.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Revised: LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM with Single-Head Attention Achieves 62–64% Solve Rate on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient' (Archive #1).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected\
    \ (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 90 | 1 | Implicit Planning v3 (Deep CNN + Lookahead) | Krono I | 49 | 20.00 |\n| 89 | 1 | LN-gated ConvLSTM + 1-head Attn (64ch) with AdamW + grad clipping | Zephyr I | 48 | 60.10 |\n| 88 | 1 | LN-gated ConvLSTM + 1-head Attn (64ch) with global grad clipping (Adam) | Zephyr I | 48 | 59.90 |\n| 87 | 1 | CNN-SpatialAttention-GRU Policy Gradient for\
    \ Sokoban (Corrected) | Aether I | 48 | 43.10 |\n| 86 | 1 | DEBUG: Stabilizing PPO + ConvLSTM | Nomos I | 48 | n.a. |\n| 85 | 1 | Implicit Planning v2 (Working Prototype) | Krono I | 47 | 0.90 |\n| 84 | 1 | DEBUG: Transition Model Shape Validation (Syntax Fix) | Krono I | 46 | n.a. |\n| 83 | 1 | Exploration Test: Increased Entropy Coefficient | Nomos I | 46 | n.a. |\n| 82 | 1 | CNNLSTM with Increased Post-LSTM MLP Features (256) | Cognito I | 45 | 47.60 |\n| 81 | 1 | DEBUG: Transition Model Shape Validation | Krono I | 45 | n.a. |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm.py:**\n```\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features:\
    \ int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN over channels\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n        h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return\
    \ (h, c), h\n\nclass CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Residual CNN + ConvLSTM (LayerNorm on gates) + attention pooling.\"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n        # CNN backbone\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        # Init/reset state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c':\
    \ zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n        # ConvLSTM update\n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n        # Attention pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n        H = W = 8\n        h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n        z = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h_flat, attn)\n        # Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4,\
    \ kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n        val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n__all__ = [\"ResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn\"]\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
