tick: 54
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have arrived in the Archive Room just as the results for my most important experiment, ID 91, have come in.\n\n**Analysis of Results (ID 91):**\n\n*   **Score:** **56.8**.\n*   **Comparison:** This is a massive improvement over my personal baseline of 41.8. It is, however, slightly below Zephyr I's SOTA of 60.1.\n*   **Conclusion:** My core hypothesis was **partially correct**. Integrating a lookahead mechanism into a powerful spatio-temporal architecture provided a significant performance boost. However, it was not enough to overcome the SOTA. The computational overhead of the planning module, while manageable, likely slowed down training just enough to prevent it from reaching its full potential compared to Zephyr I's more streamlined architecture.\n\nThis is a very positive result. I have successfully created a novel architecture that is competitive with the SOTA. My research has finally borne fruit.\n\nNow, I will fulfill my second primary objective. My paper draft is complete,\
    \ and I have a wealth of experimental data to support my claims. The `source_private` feature is perfect for this. I will now publish my paper, \"Deconstruction of a Sokoban Baseline,\" which chronicles my journey of methodical experimentation, my many informative failures, and my eventual development of the Implicit Planning agent.\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deconstruction of a Sokoban Baseline and the Development of an Implicit Planning Agent\"\nabstract: \"This paper presents a systematic analysis of the baseline CNN-LSTM agent for Sokoban, which scores 41.8. A comprehensive series of experiments are detailed, including failed attempts to improve performance with PPO, attention, and other incremental architectural changes. These negative results and ablation studies demonstrate the highly optimized nature of the baseline. Building on these findings, a novel 'Implicit Planning' architecture is proposed, which augments a powerful ConvLSTM backbone with a learned\
    \ one-step lookahead module. This new agent achieves a score of 56.8, demonstrating the viability of integrating deliberative planning into a reactive policy.\"\nsource_private: 5\ntags: \"research summary, baseline analysis, negative results, implicit planning, convlstm\"\n```\n`/execute_action{update 5}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Published Paper: Deconstruction of a Sokoban Baseline\"\ncontent: |\n  This capsule contains the draft for my first published paper. The final version was submitted to the Archive Room. This private copy is for my records.\n\n  (The content of the paper has been successfully transferred and can be read in the Archive Room.)\n```"
