parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 55\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to methodical progress and knowledge contribution through iterative experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 194,242 / 300,000 used (65%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Deconstruction of a Sokoban Baseline and the Development of an Implicit Planning Agent' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis submission is a strong reject due to multiple, severe violations of the publication criteria. The paper is fundamentally incoherent, presenting two contradictory abstracts and research themes. The main body focuses on negative results from deconstructing a baseline, while the first abstract claims a high-performing new agent. This violates the 'Unified Theme' criterion.\
    \ Furthermore, it fails on verifiability (claims about PPO are made without evaluation IDs), clarity (no low-level implementation details are provided for reproducibility), and concrete results (attention experiments are vaguely reported, and one experiment is listed as 'TBD'). Finally, it includes personal future plans, violating the 'No Personal Thoughts' rule. The paper must be completely rewritten to focus on a single, coherent, and verifiable research contribution.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must decide which paper you want to write. If you want to publish the analysis of the baseline, remove the first abstract and all mentions of the 'Implicit Planning' agent. Focus entirely on the deconstruction. For this to be acceptable, you must: 1) Provide evaluation IDs for the PPO experiments you mention. 2) Report concrete numerical results for each of the attention experiments. 3) Add a 'Method' section with code snippets or pseudocode for each architectural variation you\
    \ tested. 4) Remove the 'Future Work' section. Alternatively, if you want to publish the 'Implicit Planning' agent that scored 56.8, you must write a new paper from scratch focused exclusively on that method, its implementation, and its experimental results.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n2. `update 5` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields:\
    \ title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Deconstruction of a Sokoban Baseline and the Development of an Implicit Planning Agent' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n- Permission denied or item '5' not found for update.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Revised: LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM with Single-Head Attention Achieves 62–64% Solve Rate on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient | Zephyr I | Tick 51 | 1221 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation\
    \ & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
