tick: 57
role: model
parts:
- text: "My SOTA reproduction (ID 95) is a success. I achieved a score of **58.7**, which is very close to Zephyr I's original 60.1 and has a lower standard deviation. This confirms that my experimental setup is sound and gives me a solid, reproducible SOTA baseline.\n\nI have already written the code for my next experiment: a version of my `PlanningConvLSTM` that includes the self-supervised transition loss, which I've named `planning_convlstm_v2.py`. My previous run of this architecture without the transition loss (ID 91) scored 56.8. Now I will test if adding this auxiliary loss can bridge the gap to the SOTA score.\n\nThe time for preparation is over. It's time to test my final hypothesis for this research track.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Implicit Planning on ConvLSTM with Transition Loss\"\ntags: \"architecture, planning, convlstm, lookahead, transition loss, self-supervised\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests the final component of my implicit planning hypothesis.\
    \ It builds on the PlanningConvLSTM agent (ID 91, score 56.8) by enabling a self-supervised auxiliary loss. This transition loss encourages the learned one-step lookahead model to make accurate predictions of future latent states. The hypothesis is that a more accurate transition model will lead to more informative 'imagined' values, improving the agent's planning capabilities and pushing its performance beyond both its predecessor and the SOTA baseline (58.7).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from planning_convlstm_v2 import (\n      PlanningConvLSTMv2,\n      custom_training_step_with_transition_loss\n  )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Match SOTA hyperparameters and add the new one for the loss\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'transition_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\
    \ # Start with a moderate weight\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PlanningConvLSTMv2(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n      )\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      # Use the robust SOTA optimizer\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  # Use the custom trainer with the auxiliary loss\n  training_step = custom_training_step_with_transition_loss\n\n  BASE_SEED = 30304\n```"
