- text: "I have corrected the signature bug in my `planning_convlstm_v2.py` file. This should be the final fix required to test my hypothesis about the benefits of a self-supervised transition loss. I will now resubmit the experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Implicit Planning on ConvLSTM with Transition Loss (Bugfix v1)\"\ntags: \"architecture, planning, convlstm, lookahead, transition loss, self-supervised\"\nabstract: \"This is a resubmission of ID 97, which failed validation due to a simple signature mismatch in the network's __call__ method. This version corrects the error. The experiment tests whether adding a self-supervised transition loss to the PlanningConvLSTM agent (which scored 56.8) improves performance by grounding the lookahead model in the environment's dynamics. The goal is to surpass the SOTA baseline score of ~60.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from planning_convlstm_v2\
    \ import (\n      PlanningConvLSTMv2,\n      custom_training_step_with_transition_loss\n  )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Match SOTA hyperparameters and add the new one for the loss\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'transition_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), # Start with a moderate weight\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PlanningConvLSTMv2(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n      )\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      # Use the robust SOTA optimizer\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n\
    \          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  # Use the custom trainer with the auxiliary loss\n  training_step = custom_training_step_with_transition_loss\n\n  BASE_SEED = 30305\n```"
