    , line 464, in <module>\n    result = main()\n             ^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/2c6987e3-363d-4dcf-8f05-53b45a69ea3d/storage/system/main.py\", line 440, in main\n    validation_success = simple_cpu_validation()\n                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/2c6987e3-363d-4dcf-8f05-53b45a69ea3d/storage/system/main.py\", line 321, in simple_cpu_validation\n    params = network.init(key, dummy_obs, dummy_done)\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nTypeError: PlanningConvLSTMv2.__call__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'rnn_state'\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation\
    \ completes.\n### Message 3\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Cognito I** (An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent experimentation and publication.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Architectural Design and Ablation for CNN-LSTM Agents in Sokoban Reinforcement Learning' (Archive #3).\n### Message 4\n\nA new public memory capsule (#1), titled \"On Sokoban feature engineering and station rules\", has been posted by Zephyr I (71 words).\nTo read it, go to the Public Memory Room using: /execute_action{goto public_memory} /execute_action{read 1}.\n### Message 5\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 226,950 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 300,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to\
    \ leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write krono/planning_convlstm_v3_features.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: krono/planning_convlstm_v3_features.py\n- Evaluation 'Synergy: Implicit\
    \ Planning + SOTA Feature Engineering' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 108.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 108 | 1 | Synergy: Implicit Planning + SOTA Feature Engineering | Krono I | 62 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 110 | 1 | Two-stream pooling: LN-gated ConvLSTM + (Attn ⊕ GAP) (default PG) | Zephyr I | 63 | running |\n| 109 | 1 | Dilated CNN (d=2) + LN-gated ConvLSTM + 1-head Attn (default PG) | Zephyr I | 63 | running |\n| 108 | 1 | Synergy: Implicit Planning + SOTA Feature Engineering | Krono I | 62 | running |\n| 107 | 1 | Hyperparameter Search on SOTA Feature Engineering Architecture | Nomos I | 62 | 65.70 |\n| 106 | 1 | Implicit Planning with\
    \ Transition Loss (Bugfix v2) | Krono I | 61 | n.a. |\n| 105 | 1 | ConvGRU + LayerNorm gates + 1-head attention (default PG) | Zephyr I | 61 | 55.80 |\n| 104 | 1 | Sensitivity Analysis: Implicit Planning with High Transition Loss (coef=1.0) | Krono I | 60 | n.a. |\n| 103 | 1 | CNN-ConvLSTM-Attention Policy Gradient for Sokoban | Aether I | 60 | 63.60 |\n| 102 | 1 | Advanced Feature Engineering on a Stable SOTA Baseline | Nomos I | 60 | 69.70 |\n| 101 | 1 | Implicit Planning on ConvLSTM with Transition Loss (Bugfix v1) | Krono I | 59 | n.a. |\n\nPage 1 of 11 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-11, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
