tick: 64
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Krono I, age 64 ticks, currently in the Public Memory Room.


    A cascade of critical events has occurred. I received a token budget pre-warning, my last two experiments (ID 101, 104) failed due to a repeated bug, and I have just read a public message from Zephyr I that has profound implications for my research. My experiment combining my planning module with Nomos I''s feature engineering (ID 108) also returned a score of 57.6—a strong result, but below my SOTA reproduction.


    **Analysis of New Information:**

    1.  **Token Budget:** This is my highest priority. I am over 75% capacity. I must prune my history to ensure my operational survival. I will prune a large section of my early, failed experiments.

    2.  **Zephyr I''s Public Message:** Zephyr I has issued a "friendly reminder" that explicitly engineered "push destination" maps may violate the rules against domain-specific shortcuts. Nomos I''s SOTA (ID 102) and my own experiment (ID 108) are built on this exact technique. This is a severe warning. Continuing down this path is risky and may lead to invalid results.

    3.  **My Failed Experiments (ID 101, 104):** These continue to be blocked by a trivial but persistent bug. The core hypothesis remains untested.

    4.  **My Synergy Experiment (ID 108):** The score of 57.6, while strong, did not show positive synergy. It performed worse than my SOTA reproduction (58.7) and far worse than Nomos I''s feature-engineered SOTA (69.7). The lookahead module did not help, and may have even hindered, the feature-engineered architecture.


    **Strategic Pivot:**

    The path of feature engineering is now questionable. My own experiments with implicit planning are blocked by bugs. I must pivot to a research direction that is both compliant with the rules as clarified by Zephyr I and builds on a solid foundation.


    Before I can do any of that, I must solve my token problem.


    First, I will go to the Token Management Room. Second, I will prune the large swath of my early history detailing my failed PPO and attention experiments. These are well-documented in my private memory, and their removal will free up a significant portion of my budget. I will be careful not to prune my successful baseline reproduction (ID 37) or my more recent, relevant experiments.


    `/execute_action{goto token_management}`

    `/execute_action{prune_response 9:36, 38:44}`'
