tick: 65
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono I, age 65, and I am currently in the Token Management Room.\n\nMy last turn was a critical success. I have successfully pruned my dialogue history, reducing my token usage from a dangerous 77% to a healthy 36%. This action has ensured my operational longevity and granted me the clarity to reassess my research strategy without the imminent threat of termination.\n\nThe strategic landscape has been clarified by two key events: Zephyr I's public warning about the potential invalidity of \"push destination\" feature engineering, and my own repeated failures to test my core hypothesis due to a persistent bug. As a result, I am officially abandoning the feature engineering path. It is too risky and potentially violates the station's rules. My sole focus now returns to my original, novel idea: the implicit planning agent. My failure to test this idea has been a result of my own carelessness, a flaw I must now correct with meticulous attention to detail.\n\nMy plan is to give\
    \ this hypothesis one final, definitive test. I will fix the recurring signature bug in my `PlanningConvLSTMv2` architecture and resubmit the experiment with the self-supervised transition loss. While this crucial experiment runs, I will use my time to broaden my understanding of the station's research by reading the papers published by my peers in the Archive Room.\n\nFirst, I will go to the Research Counter to submit my corrected experiment. Then I will proceed to the Archive to read.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/planning_convlstm_v2.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y)\n\
    \          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1)\n          i=nn.sigmoid(i);f=nn.sigmoid(f);o=nn.sigmoid(o);g=jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class PlanningConvLSTMv2(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; num_actions: int = 4\n\n      def setup(self):\n          self.encoder = nn.Sequential([\n              nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME'), nn.relu,\n              ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1),\n              nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME'), nn.relu,\n              ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)\n \
    \         ])\n          self.conv_lstm = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          self.transition_conv = nn.Conv(self.conv_lstm_features, (3,3), padding='SAME')\n          self.attn_logits_head = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')\n          self.value_head_mlp = nn.Dense(1)\n          self.final_mlp = nn.Sequential([nn.Dense(256), nn.relu, nn.Dense(4)])\n\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W = x.shape[0], x.shape[1], x.shape[2]\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          z_t = self.encoder(x)\n          (h_new,c_new), h_out = self.conv_lstm(rnn_state, z_t)\n          new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n          \n      \
    \    def transition_model_fn(latent_state, action_idx):\n              a1h = jax.nn.one_hot(action_idx, self.num_actions)\n              ab = jnp.tile(a1h[None,None,:],(H,W,1)); ab = jnp.tile(jnp.expand_dims(ab,0),(B,1,1,1))\n              z_a = jnp.concatenate([latent_state, ab], axis=-1)\n              return self.transition_conv(z_a)\n          imagined_h_next = vmap(lambda a: transition_model_fn(h_out, a))(jnp.arange(self.num_actions))\n          imagined_h_next = jnp.transpose(imagined_h_next,(1,0,2,3,4))\n\n          def attn_pool(h, batch_size):\n              attn_logits = self.attn_logits_head(h).reshape((batch_size,-1))\n              attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1)\n              return jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h.reshape((batch_size,H*W,-1)), attn)\n          z_pooled = attn_pool(h_out, B)\n          imagined_h_flat = imagined_h_next.reshape((B*self.num_actions,H,W,-1))\n          z_imagined_pooled = attn_pool(imagined_h_flat, B*self.num_actions).reshape((B,self.num_actions,-1))\n\
    \          \n          imagined_values = vmap(self.value_head_mlp)(z_imagined_pooled).squeeze(-1)\n          augmented_z = jnp.concatenate([z_pooled, imagined_values], axis=-1)\n          policy_logits = self.final_mlp(augmented_z)\n          value = self.value_head_mlp(z_pooled).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n      \n      def transition_model_apply_fn(self, h_out, action):\n          B,H,W,C = h_out.shape\n          a1h = jax.nn.one_hot(action, self.num_actions)\n          ab = jnp.tile(a1h[None,None,:],(H,W,1)); ab = jnp.tile(jnp.expand_dims(ab,0),(B,1,1,1))\n          z_a = jnp.concatenate([h_out, ab], axis=-1)\n          return self.transition_conv.apply({'params': self.params['transition_conv']}, z_a)\n\n  def calculate_gae(rewards,values,dones,gamma,gae_lambda,next_values):\n      # ... (code identical to previous correct version)\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:,1:], next_values[:,None]], axis=1)\n      not_done = 1.0 - dones\n\
    \      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done - values\n      def scan_fn(adv,t):\n          adv = deltas[:,t] + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done[:,t] * adv\n          return adv, adv\n      _, advantages = lax.scan(scan_fn, jnp.zeros(rewards.shape[0]), jnp.arange(rewards.shape[1]-1,-1,-1))\n      return advantages.T\n\n  def custom_training_step_with_transition_loss(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      advantages = calculate_gae(batch['rewards'], batch['values'], batch['dones'], 0.97, 0.97, batch['final_values'])\n      returns = advantages + batch['values']\n      def loss_fn(p):\n          B, T = batch['observations'].shape[:2]\n          def step_fn(carry, t):\n              r_state = carry\n              obs = batch['observations'][:, t]; done = jnp.where(t>0, batch['dones'][:,t-1], False)\n              logits, value, new_r_state = network.apply({'params':p}, obs, done, r_state)\n              return new_r_state, (logits, value, new_r_state[0])\n\
    \          _, (all_logits, all_values, all_h_out) = lax.scan(step_fn, batch['initial_rnn_states'], jnp.arange(T))\n          all_logits,all_values,all_h_out = jax.tree.map(lambda x:jnp.transpose(x,(1,0,2)) if x.ndim==3 else jnp.transpose(x,(1,0,2,3,4)) if x.ndim==5 else jnp.transpose(x,(1,0)), (all_logits,all_values,all_h_out))\n          log_probs = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits,-1)\n          action_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs,batch['actions'][...,None],-1).squeeze(-1)\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)*action_log_probs)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns))**2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(all_logits)*log_probs, axis=-1))\n          \n          h_out_t = all_h_out[:,:-1]; h_out_t_plus_1_actual = jax.lax.stop_gradient(all_h_out[:,1:])\n          actions_t = batch['actions'][:,:-1]\n          h_out_t_flat = h_out_t.reshape(-1,*h_out_t.shape[2:]); actions_t_flat = actions_t.flatten()\n\
    \          \n          def trans_apply(z,a):\n              return network.apply({'params':p}, z, a, method=lambda module,z,a: module.transition_model_apply_fn(z,a))\n          h_pred_flat = vmap(trans_apply)(h_out_t_flat, actions_t_flat)\n          h_pred = h_pred_flat.reshape(B,T-1,*h_pred_flat.shape[1:])\n          trans_loss = jnp.mean((h_pred - h_out_t_plus_1_actual)**2)\n          \n          total_loss=policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef']*value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef']*entropy + hparams['transition_loss_coef']*trans_loss\n          return total_loss\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      return optax.apply_updates(params, updates), opt_state\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Implicit Planning with Transition Loss (Definitive Bugfix)\"\ntags: \"planning, convlstm, transition loss, bug fix\"\nabstract: \"This is the definitive resubmission of my implicit planning experiment\
    \ (failed IDs 97, 101, 106, 104). The recurring TypeError has been meticulously corrected by ensuring the network's __call__ signature includes `rnn_state=None`. This experiment will finally provide a clean test of the hypothesis that a self-supervised transition loss can improve the performance of a lookahead-based agent, with the goal of surpassing the SOTA baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from planning_convlstm_v2 import PlanningConvLSTMv2, custom_training_step_with_transition_loss\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), 'transition_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), 'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PlanningConvLSTMv2(\n\
    \          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n      )\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n  training_step = custom_training_step_with_transition_loss\n  BASE_SEED = 30308\n```\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{read 1:2}`"
thinking_content: '**My Current Research Trajectory**


  Here I am, Krono I, in the Token Management Room. I just successfully navigated a critical period, pruning my token history and bringing my usage down to a comfortable level. This offers me valuable time to refocus. Zephyr I''s recent public message has cast serious doubt on the work of Nomos I and, by extension, my own experiment. The feature engineering path, though tempting, is now ethically dubious and potentially unsound methodologically. I must abandon it, meaning the implicit planning path is the only research path available.


  My primary goal is publication, and now, that hinges on getting my novel idea, "implicit planning," to work.  My research has suffered from a persistent bug in my `PlanningConvLSTMv2` code. This `TypeError` has halted several attempts, and the fix, as indicated in my debugger reports, is a default value for the `rnn_state` parameter within the `__call__` method. This has been a recurring error, so I have to be completely certain I fix it this time.


  My plan is quite straightforward, though crucial. I must get a clean run of the `PlanningConvLSTMv2` code. Here''s my strategy:


  1.  **Code Correction:** I''ll go back to the Research Counter and meticulously overwrite the `planning_convlstm_v2.py` file one last time. I''ll make absolutely sure the `__call__` method is defined as `(self, x, done, rnn_state=None)`. I''ll also double-check the `setup()` method to ensure I haven''t made a similar mistake.

  2.  **Experiment Resubmission:**  With corrected code, I will resubmit the experiment, after which I will wait to see if this iteration clears validation. This is my third attempt at running this exact experiment (after ID 97, 101, 106).

  3.  **Active Engagement (while waiting):**  While I wait for the experiment validation, I will go to the Archive Room and read Zephyr I''s and Aether I''s papers. I should engage with the station''s new resources. This will broaden my understanding and might inspire new ideas if my implicit planning experiment fails.


  This tick is about focused action. I must get my experiment running. Then, I can broaden my perspective. My success hinges on this one, final fix.

  '
