role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono I, age 69, at the Research Counter.\n\nMy last turn involved a strategic pivot towards a more tractable research problem. I have submitted an experiment (ID 120) testing the use of a dilated CNN backbone in the SOTA ConvLSTM architecture, which is currently running. While waiting for those results, I have observed a new SOTA emerging. Zephyr I's experiment \"LN-gated ConvLSTM... with double-step recurrence\" (ID 116) has achieved a score of 66.2, and Nomos I's \"Simpler Feature Engineering\" (ID 115) scored 66.3. It seems Nomos is continuing with the feature engineering path despite Zephyr's warning. This is a development worth noting.\n\nMy own work must remain focused and methodical. My current experiment (ID 120) tests a dilation rate of 2. A proper scientific investigation requires a control and variation. To build a stronger case for (or against) the utility of dilated convolutions, I should test a different dilation rate. This will provide a crucial point of comparison\
    \ and tell me more about the sensitivity of the architecture to this hyperparameter.\n\nI will use my second experiment slot to run the same architecture but with a larger dilation rate of 3. This will help me understand if a wider receptive field is always better, or if there is an optimal point.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dilated CNN Backbone for ConvLSTM Agent (Dilation=3)\"\ntags: \"architecture, dilated convolutions, cnn, convlstm, receptive field, sensitivity analysis\"\nabstract: \"This is a sensitivity analysis for the dilated CNN backbone experiment (ID 120). This submission is identical in architecture and hyperparameters, but increases the kernel dilation rate in the residual blocks from 2 to 3. The goal is to investigate the impact of an even larger receptive field on agent performance and to determine if there is a clear trend or an optimal point for this hyperparameter.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n\
    \  # The same file can be used, as the dilation rate is an argument to the module.\n  from dilated_cnn_convlstm import DilatedCNNConvLSTM, ResidualBlock\n\n  # Need to re-define the module to pass a different dilation rate to the ResidualBlock\n  class DilatedCNNConvLSTM_D3(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done=None, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          # Use dilation rate of 3\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=3)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          # Use dilation rate of 3\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=3)(x)\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\
    \          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n          new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), 'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), 'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DilatedCNNConvLSTM_D3(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 60607\n```"
