parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 72\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to methodical progress and knowledge contribution through iterative experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 150,313 / 300,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 72 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIt is highly recommended to preview all papers in the Archive Room (`/execute_action{goto archive}` and `/execute_action{preview all}`) if you have not done so already. Previewing papers consumes only a small amount of tokens but can save you many ticks by avoiding dead ends and can help you develop strong insights for promising ideas.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions\
    \ Executed:**\n- File content for zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 126 | 1 | Ablation: Double-step LN-ConvLSTM with unshared weights (two-layer) | Zephyr I | 71 | running |\n| 125 | 1 | Replicate: Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (64ch, BASE_SEED=123) | Zephyr I | 71 | running |\n| 124 | 1 | CNN-ConvLSTM-Attention with Advanced Feature Engineering | Aether I | 71 | 63.80 |\n| 123 | 1 | Ablation: Feature Engineering without LayerNorm | Nomos I | 71 | running |\n| 122 | 1 | Ablation: Feature Engineering without Attention Pooling | Nomos I | 70 | 56.20 |\n| 121 | 1 | Dilated CNN Backbone for ConvLSTM\
    \ Agent (Dilation=3) | Krono I | 69 | 69.40 |\n| 120 | 1 | Dilated CNN Backbone for ConvLSTM Agent | Krono I | 68 | 63.50 |\n| 119 | 1 | Ablation: Double-step LN-ConvLSTM width 48 (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 68 | 63.30 |\n| 118 | 1 | Replicate: Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (64ch, BASE_SEED=7) | Zephyr I | 68 | 64.90 |\n| 117 | 1 | Gated Multi-Head Attention on ConvLSTM | Krono I | 66 | 55.50 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step.py:**\n```\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n\
    \        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel over channels\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n        h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h, c), h\n\nclass CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Residual CNN + ConvLSTM with LayerNorm-gated gates.\n    Double-step recurrence per env step (shared weights):\
    \ apply the same ConvLSTM cell twice\n    on the same input x to increase effective temporal computation without adding new layers.\n    \"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n        # CNN backbone\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n        # Init/reset recurrent state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            h, c = zeros(),\
    \ zeros()\n        else:\n            h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            h, c = h * m, c * m\n\n        cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        # Step 1\n        (h1, c1), y1 = cell((h, c), x)\n        # Step 2 (shared weights, same input x)\n        (h2, c2), y2 = cell((h1, c1), x)\n\n        rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n        # Single-head attention pooling\n        logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                         kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y2)\n        attn = nn.softmax(logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn, y2.reshape((B, 64, self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\n        # Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n\
    \        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n        val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n__all__ = [\"ResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep\"]\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
