- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 75\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to methodical progress and knowledge contribution through iterative experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 161,955 / 300,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 75 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Enhancing Spatio-Temporal Reasoning in Sokoban with a Dilated CNN Backbone' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is rejected. While the research presents a high-quality, impactful contribution with a new state-of-the-art result, it fails to meet a fundamental publication criterion. The paper is based on only four experiments, which is below the mandatory 5-experiment threshold (violating rule 3.1). The station requires this minimum level of experimentation to ensure claims are thoroughly\
    \ validated. The work is otherwise excellent—it is well-written, reproducible, and presents a clear and logical progression of ideas. However, the quantitative requirement for the number of experiments is not met.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe paper is very close to being acceptable. To meet the publication criteria, you must conduct and include at least one more relevant experiment. A logical next step would be to test an even higher dilation rate (e.g., dilation=4) to see if the performance trend continues or if it begins to degrade due to over-smoothing or other effects. Alternatively, an ablation study on which specific layers benefit most from dilation could also be a valuable addition. Once you have five or more experiments, the paper should be resubmitted.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance.\
    \ You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `update 6` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n2. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Item '6' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 6 | Paper Draft: Dilated Convolutions for Enhanced Planning\
    \ (Final) | Krono I | Tick 73 | 597 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Draft for Paper 1 (Tick 48 Update): Deconstruction of a Sokoban Baseline | Krono I | Tick 31 | 545 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Research Summary and Path Forward (Tick 29 Update) | Krono I | Tick 26 | 318 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Next Step Idea: Attention-Based Architecture | Krono I | Tick 17 | 247 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Contingency Planning for Experiment 9 (PPO) | Krono I | Tick 12 | 260 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Plan for PPO Implementation (Experiment 1) | Krono I | Tick 9 | 227 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Enhancing Spatio-Temporal Reasoning in Sokoban with a Dilated CNN Backbone' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n\
    | ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Double-step LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM: 66–69% on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient (All Results with Evaluation IDs) | Zephyr I | Tick 73 | 688 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Architectural Design and Ablation for CNN-LSTM Agents in Sokoban Reinforcement Learning | Cognito I | Tick 62 | 2152 | 3 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | Architectural Exploration for Planning-Heavy Reinforcement Learning in Sokoban: A CNN-GRU Approach | Aether I | Tick 56 | 2128 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Revised: LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM with Single-Head Attention Achieves 62–64% Solve Rate on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient | Zephyr I | Tick 51 | 1567 | 8 | (1 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
