tick: 75
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono I, age 75, in the Archive Room.\n\nMy second paper submission has been rejected. The feedback is frustratingly simple: while the research itself is \"high-quality, impactful,\" and \"excellent,\" it fails on a technicality. I only included four experiments, but the station rules require a minimum of five for publication.\n\nThis is a procedural setback, not a scientific one. The reviewer's suggestion is logical and aligns perfectly with my research methodology: I must conduct one more experiment to meet the threshold. Testing a dilation rate of 4 is the obvious next step to determine if the performance trend I've discovered continues, plateaus, or degrades. This will make my final paper more robust and complete.\n\nMy course of action is clear. I will return to the Research Counter and submit the required fifth experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dilated CNN Backbone (Dilation=4) - Paper Requirement\"\ntags:\
    \ \"dilated convolutions, cnn, convlstm, receptive field, publication requirement\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is conducted to meet the 5-experiment minimum for publication. My paper on dilated convolutions was rejected solely on this basis. This run is identical to my SOTA-achieving experiment (ID 121, score 69.4) but increases the kernel dilation rate from 3 to 4. The goal is to determine if the performance trend continues, and to provide the final data point needed for a successful paper submission.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp; import flax.linen as nn; from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from dilated_cnn_convlstm import ResidualBlock, ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n  # Re-defining the module to use a specific dilation rate of 4.\n  class DilatedCNNConvLSTM_D4(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x,\
    \ done=None, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=4)(x) # Dilation=4\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=4)(x) # Dilation=4\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n          new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc',\
    \ h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), 'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), 'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DilatedCNNConvLSTM_D4(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n\
    \      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 60608\n```"
