role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 77\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to methodical progress and knowledge contribution through iterative experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 167,649 / 300,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 77 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Dilated CNN Backbone (Dilation=4) - Paper Requirement' (ID: 131) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 69.9\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.686, 0.759, 0.661, 0.688]\nMean: 0.699, Std: 0.037\nBest trial: 2 (0.759)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n\
    \n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 131\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the missing import issue that was causing immediate crash. The code is now running without errors.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a missing import for the `jax` module. While the code imported `jax.numpy as jnp`, it did not import `jax` itself. On line 18 of the submission, the code used `jax.tree.map()` which caused a `NameError: name 'jax' is not defined`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded `import jax` to the import statements on line 1 of the submission. The complete fix was:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nimport sys; from ray import tune; import optax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp; import flax.linen as nn; from typing import Tuple, Optional\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nimport sys; from ray import tune; import optax; import jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp; import flax.linen as nn; from typing import Tuple, Optional\n```\n\nThis simple one-word addition (`import jax`) resolved the NameError and\
    \ allowed the code to run successfully. The evaluation status changed from \"failed\" to \"pending\", indicating the training is now running properly.\n\n## Verification\n- Created submission_v2.py with the import fix\n- Monitoring confirmed the code is running without crashes (timeout indicates success)\n- The evaluation file shows status \"pending\" instead of \"failed\"\n- No further errors in the execution logs\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys; from ray import tune; import optax; import jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp; import flax.linen as nn; from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\nsys.path.append('storage/krono')\nfrom dilated_cnn_convlstm import ResidualBlock, ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n# Re-defining the module to use a specific dilation rate of 4.\nclass DilatedCNNConvLSTM_D4(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int;\
    \ cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done=None, rnn_state=None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=4)(x) # Dilation=4\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=4)(x) # Dilation=4\n        \n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n        new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B,\
    \ -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), 'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), 'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return DilatedCNNConvLSTM_D4(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features']\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 60608\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 60608 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban\
    \ RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.45 | 1.75 | 4.29 | 3.47 | 7.61 | 8.31 | 10.04 | 8.68 | 10.21\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.062 | 0.273 | 0.167 | 0.500 | 0.562 | 0.706 | 0.600 | 0.727\n\nTimeout after 35301 updates (1806s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.686\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.686\nTraining time: 1819s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output\
    \ shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.43 | 1.10 | 4.21 | 7.89 | 6.81 | 6.79 | 6.74 | 10.43 | 9.57\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.231 | 0.529 | 0.450 | 0.438 | 0.444 | 0.750 | 0.667\n\nTimeout after 35501 updates (1808s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.759\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.759\nTraining time: 1821s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.56 | 1.62 | 4.28 | 3.46 | 3.52 | 5.78 | 8.00 | 9.84 | 12.70\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.062 | 0.267 | 0.214 | 0.200\
    \ | 0.357 | 0.538 | 0.684 | 0.933\n\nTimeout after 35501 updates (1808s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.661\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.661\nTraining time: 1822s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 4b00736b-95da-4236-81bd-ea117fff731e\nTotal time: 1829s\n============================================================\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.70 | 0.89 | 3.15 | 4.27 | 11.04 | 7.28 | 10.08 | 11.12 | 11.06\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.154 | 0.250 | 0.800 | 0.500 | 0.706 | 0.789 | 0.792\n\nTimeout after 35301 updates (1808s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.688\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.688\nTraining time: 1821s\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-13 13:25:49,963\t\
    INFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757741149963434231\n2025-09-13 13:25:49,976\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757741149976411183\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this\
    \ version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers\
