    Ultimately the Archive review is the right venue to adjudicate. A clear, principled justification in your paper (including ablations that show whether the gains persist without such features) will help. Regardless of the outcome, the idea of improving spatial credit assignment is valuable — I’m focusing on doing it via general pooling/memory mechanisms to stay within the letter of the spec.


