tick: 88
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono I, age 88, at the Research Counter.\n\nMy definitive synergy experiment, \"Synergy: Dilated CNN (d=5) + Wide CNN Backbone\" (ID 157), is now running. This experiment represents the synthesis of the two most powerful, rule-compliant architectural improvements discovered in the station: my own work on dilated convolutions and Cognito I's work on increasing network capacity. I am optimistic that this will result in a new SOTA.\n\nI have an available experiment slot, and my cooldown for creating a new archive document is ticking down. While I wait for the result of ID 157, which will be the centerpiece of my updated paper, I must ensure the paper itself is as strong as possible. My last successful paper was praised for its thoroughness. To that end, I should run one final ablation study to strengthen my claims.\n\nMy synergy experiment (ID 157) combines two changes: wider CNN features (64/128) and dilation (d=5). The SOTA was achieved with just wider features. My experiment\
    \ tests if adding dilation helps further. A crucial missing piece of evidence is the inverse: does adding wider features to my already SOTA-level dilated architecture help? I will test my SOTA dilated architecture (d=5, cnn=32/64) but with AdamW optimizer, to create a final, clean baseline before claiming synergy. This will make my final paper's argument logically complete.\n\n**Plan:**\nRun a final control experiment: my SOTA dilated CNN (d=5, cnn=32/64) with the AdamW optimizer to ensure perfect comparability with Cognito I's work. This will provide the final piece of evidence needed for my paper, demonstrating the isolated and combined effects of both architectural changes.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Control: Dilated CNN (d=5) with AdamW Optimizer\"\ntags: \"control, dilated convolutions, cnn, optimizer\"\nabstract: \"This is a control experiment for my final paper on dilated convolutions. It re-runs my best-performing architecture (ID 142, Dilated CNN d=5,\
    \ score 72.0) but replaces the default Adam optimizer with the AdamW configuration used by other SOTA experiments. This ensures a perfectly fair comparison against Cognito I's wide CNN SOTA (ID 147) and my synergy experiment (ID 157), providing a clean baseline to precisely measure the effect of adding network capacity.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax; import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp; import flax.linen as nn; from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from dilated_cnn_convlstm import ResidualBlock, ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n  class DilatedCNNConvLSTM_D5(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done=None, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=5)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=5)(x)\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n          new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      # Standard SOTA hparams, but with the non-wide CNN features\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DilatedCNNConvLSTM_D5(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 60611\n```"
