tick: 93
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono I, age 93, in the Archive Room.\n\nMy attempt to publish my paper has failed again due to the archive cooldown. This is a recurring frustration. The cooldown seems longer than I anticipated. I must make better use of this waiting period.\n\nMy research has established that dilated convolutions are a powerful, SOTA-level technique. My attempt to replicate Cognito I's wide CNN SOTA failed, reinforcing that my own research track is the most reliable path forward for me. The next logical step, as suggested by my own paper's reviewer, is to explore a more nuanced application of dilation.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** A \"hybrid\" dilation scheme, where different dilation rates are used in different layers of the CNN, can outperform a uniform dilation rate. Specifically, using a smaller dilation rate in the initial layers to capture fine-grained local patterns, and a larger rate in later layers to capture long-range context, will provide a more effective feature representation.\n\n\
    This is a direct and logical follow-up to my SOTA work. I will test a hybrid scheme of d=2 in the first residual block and d=5 (my best-performing rate) in the second.\n\nFirst, I must go to the Research Counter to submit this experiment. While there, I will also read the updated message in Zephyr I's paper to stay current.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/hybrid_dilation_v2.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  from dilated_cnn_convlstm import ResidualBlock, ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n  class HybridDilatedCNN(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n      dilation_rate_1: int; dilation_rate_2: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation_rate_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=self.dilation_rate_2)(x)\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n          new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n\
    \          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Dilation CNN (d=2, d=5)\"\ntags: \"hybrid dilation, dilated convolutions, cnn, receptive field, sota\"\nabstract: \"This experiment investigates a more nuanced application of dilated convolutions, as suggested by reviewer feedback on my SOTA paper. It tests a hybrid dilation scheme, applying a smaller rate (d=2) to the first residual block and a larger, SOTA-level rate (d=5) to the second. The hypothesis is that this approach will effectively capture both local and global spatial patterns, potentially outperforming a uniform dilation rate.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from hybrid_dilation_v2 import HybridDilatedCNN\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\
    \ 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), 'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), 'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate_1': tune.choice([2]), 'dilation_rate_2': tune.choice([5]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return HybridDilatedCNN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'], \n          dilation_rate_1=hparams['dilation_rate_1'], dilation_rate_2=hparams['dilation_rate_2']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 90911\n```"
