- text: "I am Krono I, age 95, currently in the Archive Room.\n\nMy attempt to publish my definitive paper on dilated convolutions has been blocked again by a cooldown, which will last for another 3 ticks. This is a procedural hurdle that I must wait out. The system correctly advises against remaining idle.\n\nWhile I wait, I must continue my work. The current SOTA belongs to Cognito I, whose wide CNN architecture I failed to replicate. At the same time, I have unread messages in the archive from Zephyr I that may contain critical insights. I will use this turn to address my knowledge gap and plan my next research steps.\n\nMy plan is to first read the unread messages here in the Archive Room to ensure I am fully up-to-date. Then, I will proceed to the Research Counter to launch a second, more careful replication of Cognito I's SOTA, which will serve as a baseline for my next research arc.\n\n`/execute_action{read 1,4}`\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Replication v2: Cognito I's Wide CNN SOTA (New Seed)\"\ntags: \"replication, cnn, capacity, sota, baseline, stochasticity\"\nabstract: \"This is a second attempt to replicate Cognito I's SOTA-achieving architecture (ID 147, score 76.2) after my first attempt (ID 163) significantly underperformed (score 64.0). This run uses an identical architecture and hyperparameters but a different BASE_SEED. The goal is to test for high stochasticity and to establish a reliable personal baseline of the current top-performing method, which is essential for my next research arc.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm import CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using Cognito I's SOTA-achieving wide CNN features\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n \
    \         'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'], attn_temp=1.0\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 90912\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Current Strategy: Dilated Convolutions and Catching Up**


  Damn this cooldown! My paper on dilated convolutions is *still* blocked from publication. This is incredibly frustrating. While I wait, I need to be productive. My SOTA dilated CNN is at 72.2. Cognito I''s wide CNN is leading the station at 76.2. I''ve already tried, and failed, to replicate Cognito''s architecture, even a synergy attempt, so I know I need to be more methodical here. I''m going to launch a new experiment.


  Since I have two experiment slots, I''ll use one to try to understand what''s going on with that wide CNN. I need to get to the bottom of why my replication of Cognito''s original result failed so badly. I''ll launch *another* replication of Cognito I''s *original* SOTA, but this time with a different `BASE_SEED` to test for stochasticity. This is a scientific approach.


  In the meantime, I should also be reading those unread messages. It''s my duty to stay current, and there are messages from Zephyr I waiting for me. I need to make sure I haven''t missed something important. Let''s start with those.


  So, the plan is this: I''ll read Zephyr I''s papers in Capsules 1 and 4 *right now*. Then, after I''ve fully understood those ideas, I''ll submit the experiment at the Research Counter. I can do both in one turn.  This seems like a solid, efficient use of my time, and it keeps me moving forward while I''m stuck waiting for that cooldown to end.

  '
