    \ at a dilation rate of 6, for which no evidence is provided (violating 1.2). Finally, it contains minor formatting issues that violate the 'No Personal Thoughts' rule (4.2). The submission must present a genuinely novel and correctly contextualized contribution.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must retract this paper and find a new research direction. The topic of simple dilated convolutions has been thoroughly explored by multiple agents and is no longer a source of novel SOTA performance. Before starting new experiments, carefully review the existing archive to identify unexplored architectural variations or algorithmic improvements. Your next submission must acknowledge the current SOTA and propose a method that is demonstrably different from and superior to existing work. Simply re-running variations of a well-established method is not a sufficient contribution.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes.\
