role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 102\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to methodical progress and knowledge contribution through iterative experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 199,764 / 300,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 102 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Synergy Test: Bottleneck Blocks + Dilated CNN (d=5)' (ID: 179) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 75.3\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.714, 0.772, 0.760, 0.765]\nMean: 0.753, Std: 0.023\nBest trial: 2 (0.772)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation_rate: 5.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 179\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - Fixed\
    \ the code crash by correcting a typo in the lineage function.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code crashed due to a simple typo in the `SynergyBottleneckDilatedNet` class from the lineage file `storage/krono/synergy_bottleneck_dilated.py`. On line 34, there was `_1` instead of `_` in the reshape operation:\n\n```python\n# WRONG (original):\nattn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -_1), axis=-1)\n\n# CORRECT (fixed):\nattn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n```\n\nThis caused a `NameError: name '_1' is not defined` during the simple CPU validation phase.\n\n## Fix Applied\nSince the bug was in an imported lineage function that could not be modified, I:\n\n1. Copied the entire `SynergyBottleneckDilatedNet` class from the lineage file into `submission_v2.py`\n2. Fixed the typo by changing `_1` to `_` on the attention pooling line\n3. Added the necessary imports for the copied class dependencies\n4. Kept all the original submission logic intact\n\nThe monitor\
    \ script confirmed the fix worked - the code now runs without crashing during the validation phase, indicating successful execution.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys; from ray import tune; import optax\nsys.path.append('storage/krono')\n\n# Import dependencies for the fixed class\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\nfrom bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\nfrom dilated_cnn_convlstm import ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n# Fixed version of SynergyBottleneckDilatedNet with the typo corrected\nclass SynergyBottleneckDilatedNet(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int = 5\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray,\
    \ jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        # 1. Synergy Backbone: Dilated Convolutions + Bottleneck Blocks\n        # Using standard 32/64 features, not the wide ones.\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \n        # 2. Standard ConvLSTM\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n        new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n\n        # 3.\
    \ Standard Attention Pooling - FIXED: changed -_1 to -1\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        # 4. Final MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Using my SOTA-achieving dilated CNN hparams (standard width)\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SynergyBottleneckDilatedNet(\n\
    \        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'], dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 10102\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs,\
    \ 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 10102 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\n\
