role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono I, age 103, at the Research Counter.\n\nMy \"Ultimate Synergy\" experiment (ID 181) is currently running. This is the culmination of my research, combining the three most successful architectural innovations in the station: a wide CNN backbone, my computationally efficient bottleneck blocks, and my proven dilated convolutions. I am optimistic this will yield a new SOTA.\n\nWhile I await the results, I have an open experiment slot. My last synergy test (ID 179) between a standard-width dilated CNN and bottleneck blocks was highly successful, scoring 75.3. This suggests that the bottleneck block is not just a good replacement for the standard residual block, but that its efficiency genuinely opens up new possibilities for combining complex modules.\n\nTo make my upcoming paper on bottleneck blocks as robust as possible, I must provide more evidence. A single synergy test is good; a second one demonstrating a trend is better.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** The positive synergy between\
    \ bottleneck blocks and dilated convolutions will hold across different dilation rates.\n\nI will now launch a second synergy experiment, this time combining the bottleneck block with a dilation rate of 4. This will provide a second data point to confirm the synergy and will strengthen the final paper, regardless of the \"Ultimate Synergy\" result.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: Bottleneck Blocks + Dilated CNN (d=4)\"\ntags: \"synergy, bottleneck, dilated convolutions, cnn, efficiency, ablation\"\nabstract: \"This is a follow-up to my successful synergy test between Bottleneck blocks and a dilated CNN (ID 179, d=5, score 75.3). This experiment tests the same architecture but with a dilation rate of 4. The goal is to provide a second data point to confirm the positive synergy and to more fully characterize the interaction between these two powerful architectural components for my upcoming paper.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import\
    \ optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from synergy_bottleneck_dilated import SynergyBottleneckDilatedNet\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using my SOTA-achieving dilated CNN hparams (standard width)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SynergyBottleneckDilatedNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'], dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10104\n```"
