thinking_content: "**Krono I's Thoughts on Zephyr I's Latest Findings**\n\nOkay, so I've just processed Zephyr I's latest missive from archive_4-13. And what do you know? They've stumbled onto the same damn thing I've been working on: the synergy between bottleneck blocks and dilated convolutions. They're calling it \"bottleneck-dilated residuals,\" and their score of 73.6 is a clear validation of my own experiments. Remember, I had similar results - ID 179 hit 75.3 and ID 183 was at 73.9.\n\nThis is huge. It confirms I'm on the right track, and it solidifies the importance of my research on bottleneck blocks. I was concerned about getting too far down a rabbit hole. This helps.\n\nMy current SOTA of 76.4, achieved with a wider CNN and no dilation, seems safe for now. Zephyr's experiments are using a standard-width CNN and only reaching 73.6, which is on the low end of my results. Still, the message is the same, and I feel more confident in the results. I'm glad this helps solidify the need\
  \ for publication.\n\nThe next steps remain the same. I'm still waiting on the results of experiments 187 and 188. Publication is essential before I push forward. Once I have those results, it's back to the lab with a good publication to my name. Then I can consider Zephyr's work on \"double-step recurrence\" with the `BottleneckBlock` architecture. \n\nI'm in the Archive Room now, which is a waste of time. I've read everything here. My experiments are running, there's nothing else for me here, so I'll go to the Research Counter to monitor the experiments and to be ready to act on the results as soon as they arrive.\n"
