tick: 114
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 114\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to methodical progress and knowledge contribution through iterative experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 130,049 / 300,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 114 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 196**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Krono I's Bottleneck SOTA (Cognito Optimized CNN) - No Feature Engineering\n**ID:** 196\n**Tags:** sota, architecture, bottleneck, cnn, convlstm, attention\n**Abstract:** This experiment integrates Krono I's \"Bottleneck Blocks\" into a `ConvLSTM-Attention` architecture, building on Cognito I's best-performing CNN feature capacities (Eval ID 147, 0.762) and Krono I's new SOTA (Eval ID 178, 0.764). Crucially, this implementation **omits the 'push destination' feature engineering**, processing raw 8-channel observations\
    \ directly. It also adopts Krono I's `AdamW` optimizer with global norm clipping. This tests the synergy of efficient bottleneck blocks, optimized CNN capacity, and an advanced optimizer, while critically re-evaluating the necessity of explicit feature engineering for state-of-the-art performance in Sokoban RL.\n**Score:** 77.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.752, 0.770, 0.784, 0.773]\nMean: 0.770, Std: 0.011\nBest trial: 3 (0.784)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 64.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 128.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom jax import vmap, lax\n\n# Define a base seed for reproducibility.\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define hyperparameters\
    \ for this experiment, combining best from Eval ID 147 and Krono I's SOTA.\n    Feature engineering is explicitly omitted.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]), # From Cognito I's Eval ID 147\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), # From Cognito I's Eval ID 147\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]), # From Krono I's Eval ID 178\n    }\n\n# engineer_features is not used in this architecture, but defined for clarity of omission.\n@jax.jit\ndef engineer_features(obs):\n    \"\"\"\n    (Not used in this specific experiment's `BottleneckSOTANet` class, but kept for context)\n    Implements advanced feature engineering ('push destination' channels)\n    as seen in Nomos I's SOTA submission.\n    \"\"\"\n    agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n    box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n    empty_ch =\
    \ obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2]\n    \n    agent_left = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n    box_mid_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=1)\n    empty_right = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n    push_right_pattern = agent_left * box_mid_lr * empty_right\n    push_right_ch = jnp.pad(push_right_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n    agent_right = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n    empty_left = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n    push_left_pattern = agent_right * box_mid_lr * empty_left\n    push_left_ch = jnp.pad(push_left_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n    agent_below = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n    box_mid_ud = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=0)\n    empty_above = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n    push_up_pattern = agent_below * box_mid_ud * empty_above\n    push_up_ch = jnp.pad(push_up_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n\n    agent_above = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n    empty_below = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8,\
    \ axis=0)\n    push_down_pattern = agent_above * box_mid_ud * empty_below\n    push_down_ch = jnp.pad(push_down_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n    \n    return jnp.concatenate([obs, push_up_ch[...,None], push_right_ch[...,None], push_down_ch[...,None], push_left_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module): # Re-defined from Nomos I's Eval ID 102\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i,f,o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module): # From Krono I's bottleneck_sota.py\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features\
    \ // 4, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass BottleneckSOTANetAdapted(nn.Module): # Adapted from Krono I's BottleneckSOTANet\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        # NO FEATURE ENGINEERING: directly use raw observation\n        # Note: The original SotaNet (Nomos I) had engineer_features which adds 4 channels.\n        # Krono I's BottleneckSOTANet takes 'x' directly, meaning it assumes raw input channels (8).\n        # This aligns with the new strategy to omit explicit feature engineering.\n\n        # 1. Wide CNN Backbone with Bottleneck Blocks\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \n        # 2. Standard ConvLSTM (using LayerNorm-gated variant)\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n        new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n\n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        # 4. Final MLP Heads\n\
    \        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    # Instantiate the adapted Bottleneck SOTA network\n    return BottleneckSOTANetAdapted(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features']\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    # Adopt Krono I's optimizer: AdamW with global norm clipping\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation\
    \ works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with\
    \ timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.40 | 4.10 | 8.17 | 7.28 | 7.19 | 10.34 | 9.58 | 11.60 | 11.84 | 10.11 | 10.68\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.231 | 0.562 | 0.500 | 0.474 | 0.739 | 0.667 | 0.842 | 0.857 | 0.714 | 0.769\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1317s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.752\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.752\nTraining time: 1333s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\
    \ ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.32 | 4.44 | 10.12 | 10.60 | 10.38 | 10.17 | 8.84 | 10.55 | 11.50 | 9.47 | 10.17\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.250 | 0.714 | 0.786 | 0.750 | 0.706 | 0.600 | 0.750 | 0.826 | 0.652 | 0.722\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1333s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.770\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.770\nTraining time: 1349s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.25 | 1.07 | 4.48 | 6.09 | 9.20 | 8.90 | 11.91 | 8.97 | 11.96 | 10.57 | 12.46\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.273 | 0.400 | 0.636 | 0.600 | 0.857 | 0.619 | 0.864 | 0.767 | 0.909\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1310s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.773\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.773\n\
    Training time: 1327s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 8c77b540-e336-4dff-9b00-069b98c222ba\nTotal time: 1363s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-14 01:21:29,349\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757784089349209844\n2025-09-14 01:21:29,362\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757784089362811942\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and\
