tick: 114
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono I, age 114, at the Research Counter.\n\nI have just reviewed Cognito I's SOTA-achieving submission (ID 196), and the key insight is astonishingly simple yet profound.\n\n**Analysis of SOTA (ID 196):**\nCognito I's innovation was not an architectural change, but a procedural one. They took my `BottleneckBlock` SOTA architecture and simply **removed the feature engineering**. The resulting score of **77.0** demonstrates that the explicit, hand-crafted \"push destination\" channels, which have been a cornerstone of SOTA research for dozens of ticks, are not only unnecessary but are actively detrimental to performance when combined with a sufficiently powerful and efficient backbone like my `BottleneckSOTANet`. The advanced architecture is capable of learning these relationships implicitly from the raw observations, and the feature engineering step was likely just adding noise or constraining the learning process.\n\nThis is a major paradigm shift for the station. The community,\
    \ myself included, has been operating under the assumption that this feature engineering was essential.\n\n**Strategic Conclusion & Plan:**\nThe path forward is now brilliantly clear. My `BottleneckBlock` is the key, but I have been applying it to a suboptimal input representation. I must now systematically test my best architectures on the raw, 8-channel observations. Zephyr I has also just published a paper on the bottleneck-dilated synergy, which I must read to inform my work.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Read the Latest Paper:** I will immediately go to the Archive Room and read Zephyr I's new paper (Archive #8) on the bottleneck-dilated architecture.\n2.  **Relaunch SOTA without FE:** I will launch my own replication of the new SOTA, combining my `BottleneckBlock` and wide CNN, but explicitly without feature engineering. This will serve as a new, clean baseline for my work.\n3.  **Relaunch Synergy without FE:** I will also re-run my most promising synergy experiment (Bottleneck\
    \ + Dilated d=5) without feature engineering. This has the potential to become the new station-wide SOTA.\n\nI am abandoning my in-progress ablation study on the bottleneck ratio (ID 199) as it is now based on a flawed, feature-engineered premise. The core of my future work must be on raw observations.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{read 8}`\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Bottleneck Wide CNN (No FE)\"\ntags: \"bottleneck, cnn, sota, replication, no feature engineering\"\nabstract: \"This is a direct replication of Cognito I's new SOTA (ID 196). It combines my Bottleneck block architecture with a wide CNN backbone and, crucially, removes the 'push destination' feature engineering that has been standard practice. The goal is to establish a personal, clean baseline for this new, more powerful paradigm.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n\
    \  from bottleneck_sota import BottleneckSOTANet\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]), 'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckSOTANet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10107\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: Bottleneck + Dilated CNN (No FE)\"\ntags: \"synergy, bottleneck, dilated convolutions,\
    \ no feature engineering, sota\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests the synergy between my two most powerful architectural innovations—Bottleneck blocks and dilated convolutions (d=5)—in the new, feature-engineering-free paradigm. The hypothesis is that without the noisy, hand-crafted input channels, this combination of an efficient block and a wide receptive field will achieve a new station-wide SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from synergy_bottleneck_dilated import SynergyBottleneckDilatedNet\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), 'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n    \
    \  return SynergyBottleneckDilatedNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'], dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10108\n```"
