role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono I, age 115, at the Research Counter.\n\nA flurry of activity has occurred. I have read Zephyr I's excellent new paper on the bottleneck-dilated synergy, which confirms my own findings. My own ablation study on the bottleneck ratio has returned a strong result. However, my attempt to launch two experiments at once failed, as I already had one experiment running. I must be more mindful of my concurrent experiment limit.\n\n**Analysis of New Results:**\n*   **ID 199 (Bottleneck Ratio Sweep):** Score **75.9**. The best performance came from a ratio of 0.25, my original setting. This is a crucial piece of data for my paper, as it characterizes the key hyperparameter of my innovation and confirms my initial choice was optimal.\n*   **Station Activity:** The pace of research is accelerating. Aether I has successfully replicated my SOTA with a score of 76.8 (ID 197). Zephyr I is now conducting scaling tests on the bottleneck-dilated architecture. The station is converging on\
    \ my `BottleneckBlock` as the new foundation for SOTA research.\n\n**Strategic Plan:**\nMy primary goal is still to publish a methodologically sound paper on my discovery. My last attempt failed because of procedural errors. I will not repeat those mistakes. The current SOTA is now **77.0**, established by Cognito I (ID 196) by removing feature engineering from my architecture. My research must now operate within this new paradigm.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Establish a Clean Baseline:** My replication of the new SOTA (ID 202: Bottleneck Wide CNN with no FE) is running. This will be the new, clean baseline for my paper.\n2.  **Test the Ultimate Synergy (Clean):** My second experiment slot is now free. I will immediately launch my ultimate synergy experiment (Wide + Bottleneck + Dilated d=5) but, crucially, **without feature engineering**. This is the most promising path to retaking the SOTA.\n3.  **Prepare for Publication:** Once these two results are in, I will have a complete,\
    \ 5-experiment study within the new non-FE paradigm, ready for a definitive, high-quality publication.\n\nI will now submit the final, critical experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ultimate Synergy: Wide+Bottleneck+Dilated CNN (No FE)\"\ntags: \"synergy, bottleneck, dilated convolutions, capacity, no feature engineering, sota\"\nabstract: \"This is my definitive synergy experiment within the new non-feature-engineered (No FE) paradigm. It combines the three most successful architectural innovations: a wide CNN backbone, my SOTA Bottleneck blocks, and dilated convolutions (d=5), all on the raw 8-channel observation. The hypothesis is that this combination will be the most powerful yet and will achieve a new station-wide SOTA, surpassing 77.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from synergy_bottleneck_dilated import SynergyBottleneckDilatedNet\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Combining\
    \ all SOTA hparams for a No-FE run\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SynergyBottleneckDilatedNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'], dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10109\n```"
