tick: 119
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono I, age 119, in the Archive Room.\n\nMy attempt to publish my definitive paper has been blocked by a cooldown. This is a procedural setback, but my research is complete and my course of action is clear. I have a 9-tick cooldown to wait out. I will not be idle.\n\nMy work has established the `BottleneckBlock` as the new foundation for SOTA architectures. The station's other leading researchers—Cognito I, Zephyr I, and Aether I—are all now actively building upon my work. This is the definition of a successful contribution to collective knowledge.\n\nThe next logical step, as suggested by Zephyr I's work on \"double-step recurrence,\" is to explore the temporal dimension. My `BottleneckBlock` optimized the spatial processing of the CNN. Zephyr I's \"double-step\" optimized the temporal processing of the ConvLSTM. The ultimate architecture must combine these two innovations.\n\n**New Ultimate Hypothesis v2:** The combination of a Wide CNN, my `BottleneckBlock`s, and Zephyr\
    \ I's `double-step` recurrence will create the ultimate architecture and achieve a score beyond the current SOTA of 77.2.\n\nThis is a high-risk, high-reward experiment. It pushes the boundaries of computational complexity, but if the efficiency of the `BottleneckBlock` is sufficient to offset the cost of the double-step, the performance could be extraordinary. This is the correct path forward.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  **Read Unread Papers:** I will first read the unread papers to ensure I have the latest information.\n2.  **Launch the New SOTA Attempt:** I will go to the Research Counter and launch this new \"ultimate\" experiment.\n3.  **Wait and Publish:** I will then use the subsequent ticks to wait out my publication cooldown, at which point I will publish my complete and final paper on the `BottleneckBlock`.\n\n`/execute_action{read 2,8}`\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/ultimate_v2.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\
    \  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  from bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\n  from dilated_cnn_convlstm import ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n  class UltimateNetV2(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # 1. Wide CNN Backbone with Bottleneck Blocks\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          \n          # 2. Double-Step ConvLSTM\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\
    \          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          \n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          # First step\n          rnn_state_1, h_out_1 = lstm_cell(rnn_state, x)\n          # Second step\n          rnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, h_out_1)\n          new_rnn_state = rnn_state_2\n\n          # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out_2)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out_2, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          # 4. Final MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ultimate Synergy\
    \ v2: Wide+Bottleneck+Double-Step\"\ntags: \"synergy, bottleneck, double-step, temporal, sota\"\nabstract: \"This is the next logical step in SOTA research. My previous work established the 'BottleneckBlock' on a wide CNN as the best spatial feature extractor. Zephyr I's work established 'double-step recurrence' as the best temporal processor. This experiment combines these two SOTA concepts into a single 'ultimate' architecture. The hypothesis is that the computational efficiency of the Bottleneck block will offset the cost of the double-step, unlocking a new level of performance and a new station-wide SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from ultimate_v2 import UltimateNetV2\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]), 'cnn_features_2':\
    \ tune.choice([128]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return UltimateNetV2(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10111\n```"
