role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 121\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to methodical progress and knowledge contribution through iterative experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 172,643 / 300,000 used (58%)\n- Agent Age: 121 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Ultimate Synergy v2: Wide+Bottleneck+Double-Step' (ID: 212) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 82.8\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.839, 0.830, 0.829, 0.814]\nMean: 0.828, Std: 0.009\nBest trial: 1 (0.839)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 64.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 128.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n\
    \n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 212\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - Fixed shape mismatch bug in double-step ConvLSTM architecture\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a shape mismatch in the double-step ConvLSTM implementation. The problem was in `ultimate_v2.py` line 32:\n\n```python\nrnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, h_out_1)\n```\n\nThe first ConvLSTM step took the CNN output `x` (128 channels) and produced `h_out_1` (64 channels). The second step then tried to use `h_out_1` as input, but the ConvLSTM was initialized expecting the same input shape as the original `x`. This caused the concatenation `[x, h]` to have the wrong channel dimension:\n\n- Expected: `[128 + 64] = 192` channels \n- Actual: `[64 + 64] = 128` channels\n\nThis triggered the Flax error: \"Initializer expected to generate shape (3, 3, 192, 256) but got shape (3, 3, 128, 256)\"\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `UltimateNetV2Fixed` class that corrects the double-step ConvLSTM by using the original\
    \ CNN output `x` for both steps:\n\n```python\n# First step - using original CNN output x\nrnn_state_1, h_out_1 = lstm_cell(rnn_state, x)\n# Second step - FIXED: still use original x, not h_out_1  \nrnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, x)\n```\n\nThis ensures both ConvLSTM steps receive inputs with consistent channel dimensions, eliminating the shape mismatch. The code now runs without crashing and can proceed to actual training evaluation.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys; from ray import tune; import optax\nsys.path.append('storage/krono')\nfrom ultimate_v2 import UltimateNetV2\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),\
    \ 'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), \n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return UltimateNetV2Fixed(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features']\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 10111\n\n# Fixed version of UltimateNetV2 with corrected double-step ConvLSTM\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\nfrom bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\nfrom dilated_cnn_convlstm import ConvLSTMCellLN\n\nclass UltimateNetV2Fixed(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray],\
    \ rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        # 1. Wide CNN Backbone with Bottleneck Blocks\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \n        # 2. Double-Step ConvLSTM - FIXED: Use original x for both steps\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        \n        lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        # First step - using original CNN output x\n        rnn_state_1, h_out_1 = lstm_cell(rnn_state, x)\n        # Second step - FIXED:\
    \ still use original x, not h_out_1\n        rnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, x)\n        new_rnn_state = rnn_state_2\n\n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out_2)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out_2, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        # 4. Final MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions\
    \ work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 10111 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling\
    \ JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.12 | 0.97 | 4.40 | 7.47 | 7.97 | 8.85 | 11.90 | 12.67 | 11.53\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.261 | 0.500 | 0.538 | 0.632 | 0.864 | 0.917 | 0.828\n\nTimeout after 35901 updates (1808s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.839\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.839\nTraining time: 1825s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 67886371 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 1.13 | 7.13 | 6.38 | 7.95 | 8.83 | 7.01 | 10.33 | 11.07\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.467 | 0.438 | 0.556 | 0.615 | 0.478 | 0.727 | 0.794\n\nTimeout after 36301\
