role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 122\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to methodical progress and knowledge contribution through iterative experimentation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 178,529 / 300,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 122 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Ultimate Baseline: Wide+Residual+Double-Step' (ID: 213) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 67.2\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.687, 0.711, 0.665, 0.624]\nMean: 0.672, Std: 0.032\nBest trial: 2 (0.711)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 64.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 128.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 213\n\n## Summary\nSuccess! Fixed the shape mismatch error in the double-step\
    \ ConvLSTM implementation. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a bug in the double-step ConvLSTM implementation in `ultimate_baseline.py` line 29:\n\n```python\nrnn_state_1, h_out_1 = lstm_cell(rnn_state, x)      # Correct: x has 128 channels\nrnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, h_out_1)  # BUG: h_out_1 has only 64 channels\n```\n\nThe ConvLSTM cell expects input with shape matching `[x_channels + h_channels]`. The first call works because `x` (128 channels) + `h` (64 channels) = 192 channels total. But the second call failed because `h_out_1` (64 channels) + `h` (64 channels) = only 128 channels, causing the shape mismatch error:\n\n`Initializer expected to generate shape (3, 3, 192, 256) but got shape (3, 3, 128, 256)`\n\n## Fix Applied\nIn `submissions/submission_v2.py`, I:\n\n1. **Copied the buggy `UltimateBaselineNet` class** from `storage/krono/ultimate_baseline.py` into the submission file as `UltimateBaselineNetFixed`\n2. **Fixed\
    \ the double-step ConvLSTM logic**:\n   ```python\n   rnn_state_1, h_out_1 = lstm_cell(rnn_state, x)\n   rnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, x)  # Use x instead of h_out_1\n   ```\n3. **Updated the `create_network()` function** to use the fixed class\n4. **Kept all other imports and functionality** unchanged since they were working correctly\n\nThe fix maintains shape consistency by using the original CNN features (`x` with 128 channels) as input for both LSTM steps, ensuring the expected 192-channel input shape (128 + 64) is preserved.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed the code runs without crashing for over 2 minutes, indicating successful execution of the training pipeline.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom ray import tune\nimport optax\nsys.path.append('storage/krono')\n\
    from ultimate_baseline import UltimateBaselineNet\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\nfrom dilated_cnn_convlstm import ResidualBlock, ConvLSTMCellLN\n\nclass UltimateBaselineNetFixed(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        # 1. Wide CNN Backbone with Standard Residual Blocks\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \n        # 2. Double-Step ConvLSTM - FIXED\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),\
    \ jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        \n        lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        rnn_state_1, h_out_1 = lstm_cell(rnn_state, x)\n        # FIX: Use x (not h_out_1) as input for second step to maintain shape consistency\n        rnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, x)\n        new_rnn_state = rnn_state_2\n\n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out_2)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out_2, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        # 4. Final MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]), 'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), \n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return UltimateBaselineNetFixed(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features']\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 10112\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation\
    \ works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 10112 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with\
    \ timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.03 | 4.32 | 7.10 | 9.39 | 7.76 | 10.20 | 10.58\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.286 | 0.500 | 0.647 | 0.524 | 0.714 | 0.750\n\nTimeout after 29301 updates (1806s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.687\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.687\nTraining time: 1820s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.40 | 0.72 | 4.42 | 7.96 | 7.64 | 6.34 | 10.36\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.250 | 0.529 | 0.526 | 0.412 | 0.731\n\nTimeout after 28501 updates\
    \ (1807s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.711\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.711\nTraining time: 1820s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.39 | 6.07 | 9.10 | 5.36 | 11.05 | 9.82 | 6.70\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.400 | 0.643 | 0.333 | 0.789 | 0.688 | 0.455\n\nTimeout after 29301 updates (1809s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.665\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.665\nTraining time: 1822s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: bd2c6e85-4c9c-4ab9-b75d-d8652bcfd01a\nTotal time: 2477s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-14 04:05:15,151\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757793915151175715\n\
    2025-09-14 04:05:15,167\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757793915167093101\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\n\
