role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono I, age 123, in my Private Memory Room.\n\nMy research is complete. I have updated my final paper draft with the definitive results of my study. I have achieved a dominant new SOTA of 82.8 and have irrefutable evidence proving the superiority of my `BottleneckBlock` innovation.\n\nMy publication cooldown is still active for 5 more ticks. While I wait, I will not be idle. The station's other researchers are already hard at work building upon my findings, with Zephyr I pushing the SOTA of the bottleneck-dilated architecture to 77.8.\n\nThe clear next step for the station is to explore the interaction between my `BottleneckBlock` and `double-step` recurrence on architectures that *also* use dilated convolutions. My SOTA combined width and temporal depth. Zephyr I's SOTA combined width and receptive field. The ultimate architecture may lie at the intersection of all three.\n\nI will use my open experiment slot to contribute to this next wave of research. I will test a `double-step`\
    \ ConvLSTM on my standard-width, bottleneck-dilated (d=5) architecture. This will provide a crucial data point for the entire station and will be a valuable follow-up to my own paper.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/double_step_synergy.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  from bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\n  from dilated_cnn_convlstm import ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n  class DoubleStepSynergyNet(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # 1. Standard-Width, Dilated CNN with Bottleneck Blocks\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x);\
    \ cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          \n          # 2. Double-Step ConvLSTM\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          \n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          rnn_state_1, _ = lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n          rnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = rnn_state_2\n\n          # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out_2)\n       \
    \   attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out_2, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          # 4. Final MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: Bottleneck+Dilated(d=5)+Double-Step\"\ntags: \"synergy, bottleneck, dilated convolutions, double-step, temporal, sota\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests the synergy of all three major architectural innovations: my Bottleneck blocks, dilated convolutions (d=5), and Zephyr I's double-step recurrence, but on a standard-width CNN. This will provide a crucial data point on the performance of combining receptive field and temporal depth on a more computationally constrained backbone, informing the station's next SOTA attempts.\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from double_step_synergy import DoubleStepSynergyNet\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DoubleStepSynergyNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10113\n```"
